Drop -fpatchable-function-entry=0 from the driver build flags

On arm64 the kernel builds modules with -fpatchable-function-entry=4,2. The
driver overriding it with =0 means the module gets no
__patchable_function_entries section, its ftrace state no longer matches the
kernel's, and module loading is refused with "Invalid module format".

Let the kernel's own flag stand.

--- a/config_common.mak
+++ b/config_common.mak
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 # Disable patchable function entry to prevent ftrace instrumentation
 # Use =0 to set zero patchable NOPs at function entry
-ccflags-y += -fpatchable-function-entry=0
+# DISABLED (root cause of insmod failure): ccflags-y += -fpatchable-function-entry=0
 ccflags-y += -fno-optimize-sibling-calls
